## 8. Scope Boundaries

### In Scope

- Enterprise data models
- Analytical data integration
- Cloud data platform reference architecture
- Metadata, lineage and data quality
- Analytical and AI-ready data products

### Out of Scope

- Replacement of operational ERP and CRM systems
- Production application development
- Payment processing implementation
- Production infrastructure deployment

## 9. Assumptions

- All business scenarios and datasets are fictional.
- Source systems expose approved extraction interfaces.
- Business domains have designated data owners.
- Architecture targets require stakeholder validation.
- Sensitive data is classified before ingestion.

## 10. Success Criteria

- Traceability from business requirements to data models.
- Consistent business entity definitions.
- Validated primary and foreign key relationships.
- Documented source-to-target mappings.
- Defined data quality and governance controls.
- Demonstrable analytical use cases using synthetic data.
